# Work Log

Daily work logs live here as `YYYY-MM-DD.md` files. Each file is a single comma-separated line of concise work phrases, suitable for copying into a time entry.

## How entries get written

Two sources append to today's file automatically:

1. **Agent post-hook** (Cursor: `~/.cursor/rules/work-log.mdc`, Claude Code: `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`) — after any task that modifies files, the agent appends a phrase describing what it did.
2. **`/write-time-entry` skill** — inspects recent git commits and appends any work not already captured.

## Customizing the format

Edit [`STYLE.md`](./STYLE.md) to change how entries are phrased, grouped, or structured. Both sources above read from that file, so changes apply everywhere.
